  "answer": {
    "text": "{\"summary\": \"Between 21:05 and 21:15 the system went from idle to a burst of traffic and job processing: request rate rose from zero at 21:07:30 to ~29 req/s at 21:11 and fell back to zero by 21:14, while pending job queue depth climbed from 0 to a peak of 1310 at 21:12 before draining to 610 by window end. Completed jobs rose steadily to 5056, latency metrics barely moved, and no errors, alerts, or deployments appeared in the window.\", \"timeline\": [{\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:05:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Window opened with an empty pending queue and no request traffic\", \"detail\": \"Pending job queue depth was 0 at window start, establishing the pre-burst baseline.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18501166\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:05:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Completed job counter stood at 3228\", \"detail\": \"The cumulative completed-jobs series began the window at 3228, the reference point for later throughput.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:07358804\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:07:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Pending queue depth first rose above baseline to 32\", \"detail\": \"The first sign of new work arriving in the job queue during this window.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18501166\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:07:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Job processing p95 sat at 0.4875s\", \"detail\": \"Worker per-job latency was essentially flat at the start of the burst, indicating no per-job slowdown.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18394865\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:07:30+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Request rate rose off zero to 7.4 req/s\", \"detail\": \"HTTP traffic began at roughly the same time the pending queue started growing.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:78613748\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:09:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"p95 request latency peaked at 0.683s\", \"detail\": \"API latency peaked only marginally above its surrounding values, so the burst did not materially degrade response times.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:33148052\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:09:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Job processing p95 peaked at 0.488s\", \"detail\": \"Worker processing time peaked a fraction of a millisecond above baseline, showing jobs themselves did not slow down.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18394865\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:11:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Request rate peaked at 29.1 req/s\", \"detail\": \"Traffic reached its maximum for the window roughly a minute before the pending queue peaked.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:78613748\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:12:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Pending queue depth peaked at 1310\", \"detail\": \"Backlog reached its maximum, indicating job enqueue outpaced worker drain during the burst.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18501166\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:13:30+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Job processing p95 returned to baseline (0.4875s)\", \"detail\": \"Per-job processing latency settled back to its pre-burst value.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:18394865\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:14:00+00:00\", \"source\": \"metrics\", \"headline\": \"Request rate returned to zero\", \"detail\": \"Incoming HTTP traffic stopped, ending the arrival side of the burst.\", \"citation_id\": \"prometheus:78613748\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:14:55.398138+00:00\", \"source\": \"logs\", \"headline\": \"Worker pod continued claiming and completing index_item jobs\", \"detail\": \"day2-worker-75d7d45556-qrrr6 logged a steady stream of 'job claimed'/'job completed' INFO lines with ~250ms durations, consistent with normal drain.\", \"citation_id\": \"loki:01763694\"}, {\"timestamp\": \"2026-08-30T21:15",
